</a:t></a:r><a:pPr indent="0" marL="0"><a:lnSpc><a:spcPts val="1800"/></a:lnSpc><a:buNone/></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="2400" dirty="0"><a:solidFill><a:srgbClr val="222222"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Times New Roman" pitchFamily="18" charset="0"/></a:rPr><a:t>To design, implement, and evaluate an automated dietary assessment system that, from a single meal photograph, decomposes mixed plates into individual food components, estimates each component's mass, grounds nutritional values in verified composition tables (IFCT 2017 / USDA), and outputs component-level and meal-level nutritional estimates with calibrated confidence intervals and selective active clarification. The system must further ensure that all outputs carry calibrated confidence intervals, enabling users to understand the reliability of each estimate. It must handle occluded, partially visible, or composite food items (e.g., sambar, mixed rice) using recipe-fraction fallbacks with explicit uncertainty labelling. The solution must be deployable on commodity CPU hardware without internet dependency, ensuring privacy, reproducibility, and accessibility for resource-constrained settings.</a:t></a:r><a:endParaRPr lang="en-US" sz="2400" dirty="0"><a:latin typeface="Times New Roman" pitchFamily="18" charset="0"/></a:endParaRPr></a:p></p:txBody></p:sp><p:sp><p:nvSpPr><p:cNvPr id="8" name="Shape 6"/><p:cNvSpPr/><p:nvPr/></p:nvSpPr><p:spPr><a:xfrm><a:off x="548640" y="2834640"/><a:ext cx="3511296" cy="2697480"/></a:xfrm><a:prstGeom prst="roundRect"><a:avLst><a:gd name="adj" fmla="val 1356"/></a:avLst></a:prstGeom><a:solidFill><a:srgbClr val="F8FAFC"/></a:solidFill><a:ln w="12700"><a:solidFill><a:srgbClr val="CBD5E1"/></a:solidFill><a:prstDash val="solid"/></a:ln></p:spPr></p:sp><p:sp><p:nvSpPr><p:cNvPr id="9" name="Text 7"/><p:cNvSpPr/><p:nvPr/></p:nvSpPr><p:spPr><a:xfrm><a:off x="713232" y="2944368"/><a:ext cx="3182112" cy="310896"/></a:xfrm><a:prstGeom prst="rect"><a:avLst/></a:prstGeom><a:noFil